33,2,,status,Mizuki,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
34,2,,status,Yumi,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
35,2,1,talk,Rin,,The pilot floor took up to nine minutes just to set up. That's huge.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Toshio,,"We are paying for empty desks. The billing is by area, not people.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Mizuki,,The survey says daylight is the biggest complaint. The plan ignores that.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Shion,,The printer side is nine decibels louder. My chair takes days to adjust.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Yumi,,"Some arrive before eight, others after ten. First-come is unfair.","{""words"":10,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Rin,,"@Toshio, if we pay for empty space, maybe we should shrink the footprint?","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Rin, re-running power costs 6,200 yen per desk. It adds up fast.","{""words"":12,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Mizuki,,"@Shion, if the window side is quiet, maybe we should prioritize that for those who need it.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Shion,,"@Mizuki, I need the quiet spot. I can't work in noise.","{""words"":11,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Yumi,,"@Rin, the morning chaos is real. We need a system that doesn't rely on speed.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Rin,,"@Yumi, exactly. If we rotate, everyone gets a turn at the good spots.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Toshio,,"@Rin, rotating means re-running power every time. That's expensive.","{""words"":9,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Mizuki,,"@Toshio, but if we fix the desks, we lock in the unfairness.","{""words"":12,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Shion,,"@Mizuki, I don't care about fairness if I'm in the noisy row.","{""words"":12,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Yumi,,"@Shion, but if we rotate, you get the window side sometimes too.","{""words"":12,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Rin,,I think rotating blocks might be the best compromise.,"{""words"":9,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Toshio,,I'm worried about the cost of constant changes.,"{""words"":8,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Mizuki,,"I prefer fixed desks, but only if we assign them fairly.","{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Shion,,I want the window side. Period.,"{""words"":6,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Yumi,,I think we need to vote on what matters most.,"{""words"":10,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
